      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "value": "\n<ol><li dir=\"ltr\">[.. .GROO]M AND BRIDE. MAY THEY BUILD AN D PROSPER.</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[... and] ninety-four years according to (the era of) documents, in the city of Damascus, which is on the rivers Amanah and Parpar.\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[...] the exalted, as the moon, established forever, an enduring witness in the sky. Selah. And the glory of our lord, crown of our head\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[... the head of the] great [Academy/Court] of the land of Israel, may the) m(emory of a) p(ious) a(nd saintly man) b(e a blessing), this marriage contract was written: There came before us\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[... and said] voluntarily and of his own choice, not being coerced, nor constrained, nor enticed, nor intoxicated\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[\u201c...] \\\\a former captive woman whom the Merciful has ransomed// [to be] to me wife and the mother of children, according to the law of Moses and Israel, in complete qiddushin. And I will serve,\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[...] faithfully.\" And this bride listened to him (accepted his proposal) and willingly consented to be married to him and to serve,</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[...] in purity and cleanness. This bride received her betrothal gift (qiddushin) in the presence of the undersigned. And [the groom] undertook\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[...her mohar of twelve zuz and a h]alf, due her, and that which remains as an additional gift, a strong, firm debt. She has no</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[right to claim one penny, as long ... and he fulfills] her [three ne]eds. And this groom took upon himself the security\u00a0 </li></ol>\n",
